/-
FAM-twin-primes: Brun's theorem and a Selberg upper bound for prime pairs,
uniform in the even shift h. Generated by scripts/assemble.py; edit
src/Twin.lean.part and src/header.lean.part, not this file.

Checked here (Lean 4.35.0, Mathlib 56a00585, axioms propext, Classical.choice,
Quot.sound):
* `brun_summable`: the sum of 1/p over primes p with p + 2 prime converges.
* `twinCount_le`: #{p < N : p, p + 2 prime} ≤ 2^28 N / (log N)^2 for N ≥ 2.
* `pairCount_le_log`: for every even h > 0 and N ≥ 2,
  #{p < N : p, p + h prime} ≤ 2^13 K(h)^2 N / (log N)^2, K(h) = ∏_{p ∣ h} p/(p-1).
* `pairCount_le_uniform`, `pairCount_le`: the explicit Selberg-sieve inequalities
  behind these (level w^4, error term w^16).

Not checked here: nothing that the statements depend on. The constants are far
from optimal, and K(h)^2 is weaker than the singular series ∏_{p ∣ h, p > 2} (p-1)/(p-2).

The first part of this file is a verbatim copy (up to the edits listed in
scripts/assemble.py) of the Selberg sieve files of PrimeNumberTheoremAnd
(Mathlib/NumberTheory/Sieve/{AuxResults,Basic,Selberg,SelbergBounds}.lean,
commit 127b50e3 of 2026-10-19, Apache 2.0, author Arend Mellendijk). They are
inlined because the checker accepts one file; they are checked here as well.
-/
